---
source: crates/langmeld-meta/tests/load.rs
expression: "refused_text(&format!(\"{HEAD}rule File = A\\nrule A = A \\\"+\\\" ident | ident\\nrule Empty = (ident?)*\\n\"))"
---
error[LM-G002]: `A` can start with itself (A -> A), so parsing it would never take a token
 --> t.langmeld:5:6
  |
5 | rule A = A "+" ident | ident
  |      ^
  = note: In technical terms: this is left recursion, which a parser that reads from left to right cannot handle.
  = note: To fix this, move operators into an `expr` block.

warning[LM-G006]: `Empty` is never used
 --> t.langmeld:6:6
  |
6 | rule Empty = (ident?)*
  |      ^^^^^
  = note: To fix this, use it, or remove it.
